  "editorial": "chain.from_iterable is the lazy one-level flatten. Building the result list is the caller's materialization. A nested comprehension does the same work. The chain version does not need the inner lists to be concatenated by hand.",
  "reference_solution": "def solve(rows):\n    from itertools import chain\n    return list(chain.from_iterable(rows))\n"
